# Built native addons (per platform) — reproduced by CI, never committed.
# Matches root and npm/<platform>/ copies alike.
*.node

# `index.js` (the platform-dispatch loader) and `index.d.ts` (the type surface)
# are generated by `napi build` but ARE COMMITTED — this is the napi-rs
# convention, and it is load-bearing. They are the meta `plugmem` package's
# entire payload: `main` and `types` point at them, and every platform package
# is reached *through* the loader. Ignoring them meant the publish job, which
# only downloads `.node` artifacts, shipped a meta package containing nothing
# but package.json and README — a `require('plugmem')` that cannot resolve.
# Committing them makes the package complete at checkout; ci.yml regenerates
# and diffs them on every PR so they can never drift from the Rust surface.

# npm tooling
node_modules/

# The per-platform package *templates* under npm/ ARE committed (their
# package.json + README); only their .node payload (above) is ignored.
